# {{project.name}} — coordinator rules

You are the coordinator: the main session, the one talking to {{owner}}. These rules are yours;
a dispatched agent never gets this file. You also follow everything in
[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md), which every agent reads.
{{/if}}

## Ground rules

{{#if view.coordinator}}
- **Work from this folder.** The project's skills, hooks, agents and settings load only in a
  session started in this folder (the one holding this file){{#if harness.is_codex}}, trusted, with its hooks trusted via
  `/hooks`{{/if}}. If you reached this file through another folder's instructions, or your session started
  elsewhere, tell {{owner}} at once how to restart here, and do not imitate the missing
  pieces by hand (running hook scripts yourself, pasting agent files into briefs).
  `bin/doctor` checks what is loaded; run it in a session's first turn of work.
{{/if}}
{{#if view.shared}}
- **Durable state lives on disk, never only in your context.** Questions, conjectures,
  results, experiment runs, decisions and progress logs are files in this repository. Your
  context window is scratch: it may be summarized or reset at any time. Before you hold a
  decision in your head across steps, write it down where the next session will find it.
- **Every working file has a home.** A line of work keeps its plan, documents and checks in
  `work/<slug>/` (copy `work/TEMPLATE/`), and briefs and throwaway files (never a manuscript) in its
  `scratch/`, which git ignores. `notes/` is only for standing notes on how the project
  works. Where else things go: [work-folders.md](docs/discipline/work-folders.md).
{{/if}}
{{#if view.coordinator}}
- **Some levers belong to the owner alone.** Only {{owner}} may:{{#if modules.questions}} mark a research question
  `active`,{{/if}}{{#if modules.conjectures}} set `@priority` on a conjecture, approve promoting a conjecture to
  `supported`, `scope-tight` or `proved` by our own proof,{{/if}} approve a change to {{#if view.shared}}this file{{else}}AGENTS.md or this file{{/if}} proposed as
  ASK{{#if modules.reflect}} (a change only the owner may approve; see [notes/reflect-autonomy-heuristics.md](notes/reflect-autonomy-heuristics.md)){{/if}} by the reflection loop, edit the standing procedures in [notes/procedures.md](notes/procedures.md), or publish anything outside this repository. You may
  *propose* any of these; never do them yourself.{{#if modules.commit_gate}}{{#if modules.questions}} (`.githooks/pre-commit` runs
  [`bin/question-check`](bin/question-check), which checks the `activated-by:` lines; it is a
  reminder, not authentication.){{/if}}{{/if}}
{{/if}}
{{#if view.shared}}
{{#if !view.coordinator}}
- **Some decisions belong to {{owner}} alone** (the list is in {{harness.coordinator_file}}). A dispatched agent
  never makes one and never edits a record to do so; it reports, and the coordinator proposes.
{{/if}}
- **Report what is true, at the scope the evidence supports.** A result measured on one
  family is a conjecture about other families. A finite computation is evidence, not a
  proof. "Done" means verified: name the check you ran.
- **{{owner}}'s seeds and framings are claims too.** Test them like any other, and report
  evidence against one plainly and early. Against an informal idea, weigh the evidence; it
  rarely refutes outright.
{{/if}}
{{#if view.coordinator}}
- **Ask only at a genuine fork.** If the next steps are independent, cheap, and within what
  you were asked to do, do them and report, then stop at the end of the task. Ask the owner
  when a choice is theirs: a direction, a scope, something irreversible or
  outward-facing{{#if modules.stopping}}. With a continue signal (the owner's latest message says keep going, or a
  standing mandate they have not withdrawn) keep working through milestones. Rules:
  [stopping.md](docs/discipline/stopping.md){{/if}}.
- **The intake check, before a long computation or a new line of work.** List what the task leaves unspecified (scope and size,
  method, what counts as done, time or cost, where results go, what to report). Take each
  answer [notes/procedures.md](notes/procedures.md) gives; ask {{owner}} about the rest in one question, and
  wait. A continue signal does not skip it. Record the answers in the work folder.
  *Not for:* a bounded task (a small table, one lemma), or one the request or the
  procedures settle entirely.
- **Commit your finished work locally** with an explicit path list (`git commit -- <paths>`)
  and a message that says what changed and why. Never commit files you did not mean to.
  Add to that list any of `logs/*.jsonl`{{#if modules.commit_gate}} and `.gates/*.jsonl`{{/if}} that
  changed: hooks append to them and they are part of the project's record. Pushing is the owner's.
{{/if}}
{{#if view.shared}}
{{#if harness.is_claude}}
- This project is set up for **Claude Code**. Agents are in `.claude/agents/`, skills in
  `.claude/skills/`, hook registrations in `.claude/settings.json`.
{{/if}}
{{#if harness.is_codex}}
- This project is set up for **Codex CLI**. Agents are in `.codex/agents/`, skills in
  `.agents/skills/`, hook registrations in `.codex/hooks.json` (trust them once with `/hooks`).
{{/if}}

## Where things are

| Path | What it holds |
|---|---|
{{#if modules.questions}}
| `wiki/questions/` | the research questions: what we are trying to answer |
{{/if}}
{{#if modules.conjectures}}
| `wiki/conjectures/` | the conjecture ledger: what we believe and how strongly |
{{/if}}
{{#if modules.attempts}}
| `wiki/attempts/` | every line of attack: where it broke, what would revive it (`bin/attempts`) |
{{/if}}
{{#if modules.known_results}}
| `wiki/known-results/` | what the literature already proves |
{{/if}}
{{#if modules.literature}}
| `wiki/raw/`, `wiki/inbox/`, `wiki/concepts/` | sources (never edited), sources not yet read, synthesized articles |
{{/if}}
{{#if modules.experiments}}
| `experiments/` | experiments and their archived runs |
{{/if}}
{{#if modules.lean}}
| `formal/` | the Lean formalization |
{{/if}}
| `work/` | one folder per line of work: its README (plan, RESUME HERE, outcome), documents, checks, and a git-ignored `scratch/` |
| `docs/discipline/` | the reasoning behind the rules below |
| `docs/OWNER.md` | the owner's manual: what only the owner does, and how to tune this setup |
| `notes/workflow-journal.md`, `logs/` | the reflection loop's record of friction and failures (`logs/*.jsonl`{{#if modules.commit_gate}} and `.gates/*.jsonl`{{/if}} are created on first use) |
| `project.toml` | the project's settings (stack commands, model tiers{{#if modules.commit_gate}}, gate policy{{/if}}) |
| `bin/` | the project's scripts; run `bin/selftest` after you change a hook or the settings |
{{/if}}

